    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/esbshedkitrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=016257": {
      "title": "Lecturer in Computing (Animation) #IJ",
      "description": "Lecturer in Computing (Animation) #IJ Vacancy Description : The Department of Visual and Human-Centred Computing at Dundalk Institute of Technology is seeking to appoint a Lecturer in Computing (Computer Animation). The successful candidate will contribute to teaching, curriculum development, assessment and research across undergraduate and postgraduate programmes, with particular expertise in areas such as 3D modelling and animation, character animation, visual effects, game art and real-time rendering. The role involves supporting student learning, engaging in applied research, contributing to programme development and maintaining strong links with industry. The successful candidate will also be expected to deliver teaching through face-to-face, online and blended learning formats, including scheduled online classes during evening hours, in accordance with departmental requirements. Job Title : D011-Lecturer Grade Vacancy ID : 016257 Vacancy Type : Academic"
    },
